    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71067.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "And talk about money. Ross amassed a fortune estimated by Forbes magazine at 2.5 billion dollars. Much of that came from just buying up companies in struggling industries like I indicated. So interesting hearings going on today. Meanwhile, the other hearing going on is for health and human services, Tom Price and Richard Trunka, the labor federation, issued an email yesterday to sign a petition to stop him from becoming the next head of HHS. And this is what it reads, Congressman Tom Price is wholly unsuited to serve as Secretary of the Department of Health and Human Services and Agency that has a profound impact on the health and security of every American family. Representative Price has fought to weaken the very programs that he has been nominated to oversee. I strongly urge you to oppose the confirmation of Representative Price. President-elect Donald Trump promised he was not going to change Medicare if elected, but his pick for this department, Tom Price, has been a vocal supporter of dismantling Medicare and leaving seniors to pick up the tab. More than 55 million Americans currently depend on Medicare, and that's not counting the working people or depending on it when they retire in the future. We cannot let anyone undermine it. So we're calling out our members of Congress to stand against Price's nomination for Secretary of Health and Human Services. And if you go to the Labor Federation website or go to peoplepower.org, you can sign that petition. That's on behalf of Richard Trump, the President of the Labor Federation. All right, we're going to take a break. When we come back, Joe Thayer of the Sheet Metal Workers coming up next, you are listening to America's workforce.",
