  {
    "episode_id": 71067,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71067.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 78,
    "turn_text": "Yes, currently, the way we structure the application dates, we take applications here at our office in Parma 12525 Corporate Driving Parma on the second Monday of every month. So coming up, we are going to have February 13th, March 13th, April 10th, May 8th, June 12th, and July 10th. Again, second Monday of the month, just make it easier. And that's from 1130 AM to 6 PM. No appointment necessary can come in anytime. And what you need to bring with you is a copy of your GED or high school diploma. And if by chance you don't have either of those high school transcripts will be fine. And then you can bring in the other document as you're able to get it. You'll also need a valid photo ID. And then you'll need $10 cash application fee. At that time, that's really all you need. But one thing I do suggest is if you do have some construction background experience, especially trade related, And you have some certifications or training certificates. You can bring those in at that time. And we will copy those. And as we build your file, we'll already have that on hand. It kind of makes things a little easier for us. So you'll go through a lot of the application. And then at that point, we give you the information for the next step, which is the entrance exam, which is essentially a five-part aptitude test. And there's math. comprehension, mechanical reasoning, spatial relations. We give you resources to study for that test as well as a practice test. There's some online resources. You can go to your library.",
