  {
    "episode_id": 71067,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71067.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 112,
    "turn_text": "Thank you very much, Senator Warren. First, thank you to all of you for coming. I know it's not easy to be here, and we are very proud of all of you and the ability to showcase your voices, which the regular process of hearings has chose to shut out. And I want to thank Senator Warren and working with our Democratic Housing Communications Committee and with our lead Democrat on the regular committee, the Help Committee. Senator Warren and her staff have done an incredible job of coordinating, and we thank you very much for doing that. So we're anxious to hear from all of you, but know that for us, we are going to do everything possible to give you an opportunity and the people across the country to have an opportunity to share their voices, feelings and concerns about this cabinet being put together, as well as showing through our votes how we can reflect your concerns. Thank you.",
